# art_source/ is the workshop. Track the small, meaningful artefacts; keep the
# bulk out of git. Everything ignored here still lives on the Drive, which is
# itself backed up — this only keeps the repository honest about what is ours
# and what is recoverable.

# Third-party donor art, copied from the owning mod. Not ours to redistribute,
# and regenerable in one command:
#     python Source/grab_source_art.py <defName>
*/restored/

# The untouched files as they came back from the image model. Multi-megabyte,
# and preserved automatically by fit_sprite.py so a bad fit can always be redone
# with different parameters. Keep them on disk; do not put them in git.
*/*/_raw/
*/restored_regenerated/

# Multi-facing sheets as they come back from the model, BEFORE cutting. One per
# attempt, ~1.6 MB each, and an attempt is cheap — 13 of these accumulated for a
# single machine in one afternoon and buried the two files that matter. The
# product is the cut per-facing PNG in the tier folder; a sheet is scaffolding.
# Swept 2026-08-12 after the owner could not find anything in here.
*/sheets/*_SHEET.png
# ...except the donor composite that the pipeline READS. README.md and every
# BRIEF hand this to the image model as the reference. It is an input, not an
# output, and it must stay.
!*/sheets/SOURCE_SHEET.png

# Tracked deliberately (do not add to this file):
#   MANIFEST.json     the measurements every check depends on
#   BRIEF.md          the generated commission brief
#   HOLES.txt         what is still missing
#   CONTACT_SHEET.png the review sheet
#   wrecked/*.png     the conformed sprites — the actual product
#   kludged/*.png
